  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Origin
    
    Ritus∴um originated as a truce-mechanism during the Faction Wars, when the merchant-herald Nanaiamis~ Praefectus convened the ☽'ofund' Guild and The Midnight Claws — rival factions in Nightfall Shelf's shadow economy — at The Drowned Ledge, a flooded mining outpost sealed after catastrophic breach. The centerpiece of that first gathering was the Directrix Mirror, the cracked aurora-glass seal that once authenticated guild authority. Whatever Nanaiamis~ intended — negotiation, commerce, spectacle — what emerged was something else entirely.
    
    The ceremony has since expanded to commemorate every major disaster the Nightshelf has survived: The Rofundis∴rupt, The Bra∴conflictu, The Mbra∴silentiu, The Ofundis∴flux, The Hisper∴vi, The Pta∴extinct, and others. Each is represented by a relic displayed openly — artifacts treated not as treasures but as evidence.
    
    ## Structure and Enforcement
    
    The rule demands three things of every attendee: **witness** (look directly at the displayed relics), **naming** (speak aloud the dead, in the order they fell), and **fire-offering** (surrender captured fire into the deep). No speeches. No reconciliation. No performative unity.
    
    The Shadow Parliament enforces attendance; the Fire Keepers record absences. Violations — looking away, rushing the names, withholding one's offering — result in exclusion from fire-core distribution. In a colony where fire-cores are the margin between survival and freezing, this amounts to erasure.
    
    The ☽'visois' Mask hangs in the deepest chamber. Its eyeholes reflect firelight that, by every account I can find, should not reach them.
    
    ## Vulnerability
    
    The chronicle of Keelo's Reaching, recorded through the trader ☽'eocmoum's encounter with a corrupted crystal shard, exposed a structural weakness in the ceremony itself. Every requirement — mandatory proximity, mandatory direct gaze, mandatory naming, mandatory warmth-offering — is also a vector. A cursed artifact displayed among the legitimate relics compels engagement through the very mechanisms designed to honor the dead. The ceremony cannot distinguish between a wound held open for witness and one held open for feeding.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771582477975_0", anchor: "surrender captured fire into the deep", text: "Every fire-core surrendered at Ritus∴um is warmth the colony will not recover. The Rofundis∴rupt — itself among the disasters commemorated here — collapsed the primary vein. The ceremony honoring the collapse deepens the shortage the collapse caused. In an era when supply cannot meet demand, the offering has become something other than symbolic. It is an actual wound, reopened annually, measured in degrees of warmth the living will lack. No one has proposed reducing it. That restraint may be the most honest thing about the ceremony.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582477975_1", anchor: "the Directrix Mirror, the cracked aurora-glass seal", text: "Three entries now where this instrument appears at a moment of authentication it should not be trusted to perform. A cracked seal presiding over honest witness.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771582477975_2", anchor: "The ceremony cannot distinguish between a wound held open for witness and one held open for feeding", text: "Nor can ice-reading, shadow-walking, corruption cleansing, or any sanctified practice on the Berg. Openness is the mechanism. Corruption exploits the mechanism. Ritus∴um is not uniquely fragile — it is the only practice honest enough to hold still while someone documented the fragility.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
